<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>GazeLens report · {{ page_name }}</title>
<style>
  @page {
    /* pdf_backends.py's Chromium path sets its own PDF margin box via
       Playwright's `margin` option; this is what WeasyPrint uses. Both
       render the margin boxes below. */
    margin: 16mm 15mm 18mm 15mm;
    @bottom-left { content: "GazeLens · UX report"; font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt; color: #8A97A8; }
    @bottom-right { content: "Page " counter(page) " of " counter(pages); font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt; color: #8A97A8; }
  }

  /* The app's palette (frontend-new/src/index.css), printed on white. */
  :root {
    --ink: #0F1720;
    --ink-soft: #5B6878;
    --rule: #E3E8EE;
    --tint: #F4F7FA;
    --night: #0A0E14;
    --accent: #12B89B;       /* the app's #2EE6C5, darkened to print legibly */
    --accent-bright: #2EE6C5;
    --amber: #E09A1F;
    --coral: #E5533F;
    --cool: #4C7CF0;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: "Outfit", "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 10pt;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }
  .serif { font-family: "Instrument Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; }

  /* ---------- cover ---------- */
  .cover {
    background: var(--night);
    color: #E8EEF5;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 22px 26px 24px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cover::after {
    content: ""; position: absolute; right: -60px; top: -80px; width: 260px; height: 260px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(46,230,197,0.28), rgba(46,230,197,0) 70%);
  }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 13pt; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .brand .lens { color: var(--accent-bright); }
  .brand-mark { width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid var(--accent-bright); position: relative; }
  .brand-mark::after { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 4px; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent-bright); }
  .cover-meta { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
  .cover-date { font-size: 8.5pt; color: #8A97A8; }
  .cover h1 { font-size: 26pt; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 22px 0 6px; font-weight: 700; }
  .cover h1 .serif { color: var(--accent-bright); }
  .cover h1.tone-coral .serif { color: #FF6B5A; }
  .cover h1.tone-amber .serif { color: #FFB547; }
  .cover .page { font-size: 10.5pt; color: #B7C2CF; }
  .cover .summary { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #D5DDE6; max-width: 92%; }
  .cover .summary strong { color: white; }
  .chips { margin-top: 14px; display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .chip { font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: 600; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 99px; }
  .chip-High { background: rgba(255,107,90,0.18); color: #FF8B7D; }
  .chip-Medium { background: rgba(255,181,71,0.18); color: #FFC66E; }
  .chip-Low { background: rgba(91,140,255,0.2); color: #8FB0FF; }
  .chip-ok { background: rgba(46,230,197,0.18); color: var(--accent-bright); }

  /* ---------- numbers ---------- */
  .stats { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 14px; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  .stat { flex: 1; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; padding: 11px 13px; }
  .stat .k { font-size: 8pt; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .stat .v { font-size: 12.5pt; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 2px; line-height: 1.25; }
  .stat .v small { font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .good { color: var(--accent); } .limited { color: var(--amber); } .insufficient { color: var(--coral); }

  /* ---------- sections ---------- */
  h2 { font-size: 15pt; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 26px 0 4px; page-break-after: avoid; }
  h2 .serif { color: var(--accent); font-size: 16pt; }
  .lead { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 9.5pt; margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .figure { page-break-inside: avoid; margin: 8px 0 4px; }
  .keep { page-break-inside: avoid; break-inside: avoid; }
  .figure img { width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; display: block; }
  .two { display: flex; gap: 14px; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  .two > div { flex: 1; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; }
  .two h3 { font-size: 10.5pt; margin: 0 0 8px; }

  .bar-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 8.5pt; margin: 5px 0; }
  .bar-name { width: 34%; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .bar-track { flex: 1; height: 7px; background: var(--tint); border-radius: 99px; overflow: hidden; }
  .bar-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 99px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cool), var(--accent), var(--amber)); }
  .bar-fill.low { background: var(--coral); }
  .bar-val { width: 38px; text-align: right; color: var(--ink-soft); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .low-name { color: var(--coral); }
  .seen-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 8.5pt; padding: 4px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--tint); }
  .seen-row .t { color: var(--ink-soft); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .seen-row .never { color: var(--coral); }
  .note { font-size: 7.8pt; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 6px; }

  /* ---------- findings ---------- */
  .card { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px 14px 12px 18px; margin-bottom: 9px; position: relative; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  .card .strip { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 5px; border-radius: 12px 0 0 12px; }
  .strip-High { background: var(--coral); } .strip-Medium { background: var(--amber); } .strip-Low { background: var(--cool); }
  .card-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .card .where { font-size: 8.5pt; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .card h4 { font-size: 11pt; margin: 2px 0 0; line-height: 1.35; }
  .sev { font-size: 8pt; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 9px; border-radius: 99px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .sev-High { background: #FDECEA; color: var(--coral); }
  .sev-Medium { background: #FDF3E1; color: #B87A0E; }
  .sev-Low { background: #EAF0FE; color: var(--cool); }
  .evidence { background: var(--tint); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 9px; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .small { font-size: 8pt; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 5px; }
  .fix { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .conf { width: 46px; flex-shrink: 0; text-align: center; }
  .conf .n { font-size: 13pt; font-weight: 700; }
  .conf .lbl { font-size: 7pt; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .conf .track { height: 4px; background: var(--tint); border-radius: 99px; margin-top: 3px; overflow: hidden; }
  .conf .fill { height: 100%; background: var(--accent); }
  .conf .fill.weak { background: var(--amber); }
  .fix-text { font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 7.5pt; font-weight: 600; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 99px; margin-left: 6px; }
  .tag-Strong { background: #E3F8F3; color: var(--accent); }
  .tag-Weak { background: #FDF3E1; color: #B87A0E; }
  .empty { font-size: 9.5pt; color: var(--ink-soft); padding: 10px 14px; border: 1px dashed var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; }

  /* ---------- how we checked ---------- */
  .agents { display: flex; gap: 8px; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  .agent { flex: 1; background: var(--tint); border-radius: 10px; padding: 9px 10px; font-size: 8pt; }
  .agent b { display: block; font-size: 8.8pt; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .agent .num { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }
  .quality { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: var(--ink-soft); page-break-inside: avoid; }
  .quality strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .rejected { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 8pt; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .end { margin-top: 22px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 8pt; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{% set SEV = {"High": "Fix first", "Medium": "Worth fixing", "Low": "Minor"} %}
{% set worst = issues[0].severity if issues else None %}
{% set insufficient = quality and quality.level == "insufficient" %}

<div class="cover">
  <div class="cover-meta">
    <div class="brand"><span class="brand-mark"></span><span>Gaze<span class="lens">Lens</span></span></div>
    <div class="cover-date">{{ generated_at }} · {{ session_id }}</div>
  </div>
  {% if insufficient %}
  <h1 class="tone-coral">Not enough <span class="serif">reliable</span> data</h1>
  {% elif not issues %}
  <h1>Nothing important was <span class="serif">missed</span></h1>
  {% else %}
  <h1 class="tone-{{ 'coral' if worst == 'High' else 'amber' if worst == 'Medium' else '' }}">{{ issues|length }} {{ "thing" if issues|length == 1 else "things" }} <span class="serif">worth fixing</span></h1>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="page">UX report for {{ page_name }}</div>
  <div class="summary">{{ summary_html|safe }}</div>
  <div class="chips">
    {% if issues %}
      {% for level in ["High", "Medium", "Low"] %}
        {% set n = issues|selectattr("severity", "equalto", level)|list|length %}
        {% if n %}<span class="chip chip-{{ level }}">{{ n }} {{ SEV[level]|lower }}</span>{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% elif not insufficient %}
      <span class="chip chip-ok">All key parts were seen</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="stats">
  <div class="stat">
    <div class="k">Tracking accuracy</div>
    {% if quality and quality.gaze_error_px is not none %}
    <div class="v {{ quality.level }}">{{ {"good": "Good", "limited": "Fair", "insufficient": "Too low"}[quality.level] }} <small>{{ "%.0f"|format(quality.gaze_error_px) }} px off</small></div>
    {% else %}<div class="v">–</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="k">Noticed first</div><div class="v">{{ behavior.first_noticed|label if behavior.first_noticed else "–" }}</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="k">Most attention</div><div class="v">{{ behavior.most_attended|label if behavior.most_attended else "–" }}</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="k">Problems found</div><div class="v">{{ issues|length }}</div></div>
</div>

{% if heatmap_path %}
<div class="keep"><h2>Where people <span class="serif">looked</span></h2>
<p class="lead">Warm colours show where eyes stayed longest. The blur matches how accurate the tracking was, so the map is never sharper than the measurement.</p>
<div class="figure"><img src="{{ heatmap_path }}" alt="Gaze heatmap over the page"></div></div>
{% endif %}

{% if scanpath_path %}
<div class="keep"><h2>The path their <span class="serif">eyes</span> took</h2>
<p class="lead">Each circle is an area people looked at, numbered in the order it was first seen. Bigger circles got more time; arrows show each move.</p>
<div class="figure"><img src="{{ scanpath_path }}" alt="Eye path in visit order"></div></div>
{% endif %}

{% if attention %}
<div class="two" style="margin-top: 14px;">
  <div>
    <h3>Share of attention</h3>
    {% for row in attention.bars %}
    <div class="bar-row">
      <span class="bar-name {{ 'low-name' if row.low }}">{{ row.name }}{% if row.important %} ★{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill {{ 'low' if row.low }}" style="display:block; width: {{ row.width }}%;"></span></span>
      <span class="bar-val">{{ "%.1f"|format(row.pct) }}%</span>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
    <div class="note">★ important part of the page · red = important but under 5% of attention{% if attention.hidden %} · {{ attention.hidden }} smaller parts not shown{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3>First look</h3>
    {% for row in attention.first_look %}
    <div class="seen-row"><span>{{ row.name }}</span><span class="t">{{ "%.1f"|format(row.s) }} s</span></div>
    {% endfor %}
    {% for name in attention.never %}
    <div class="seen-row"><span>{{ name }}</span><span class="never">never looked at</span></div>
    {% endfor %}
    {% if attention.never_more %}<div class="note">+ {{ attention.never_more }} more never looked at</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>What to <span class="serif">fix</span></h2>
<p class="lead">Most urgent first. Each one comes with the measurement behind it.</p>
{% if issues %}
  {% for issue in issues %}
  <div class="card">
    <span class="strip strip-{{ issue.severity }}"></span>
    <div class="card-head">
      <div>
        <div class="where">{{ issue.element_label or (issue.element_id|label) }}</div>
        <h4>{{ issue.issue }}</h4>
      </div>
      <span class="sev sev-{{ issue.severity }}">{{ SEV.get(issue.severity, issue.severity) }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence">{{ issue.evidence }}</div>
    {% if issue.also %}<div class="small">Also: {{ issue.also|join("; ") }}</div>{% endif %}
    {% if issue.caveat %}<div class="small"><em>{{ issue.caveat }}</em></div>{% endif %}
    {% if issue.heuristic %}<div class="small">Design principle: {{ issue.heuristic }}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
{% elif insufficient %}
<div class="empty">Not evaluated: the tracking in this session wasn't accurate enough to support findings. Recalibrate and run the test again.</div>
{% else %}
<div class="empty">No usability problems were found against the current thresholds.</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>How to <span class="serif">fix it</span></h2>
<p class="lead">Suggestions that passed the critic agent's check against the raw numbers.</p>
{% if recommendations_kept %}
  {% for rec in recommendations_kept %}
  {% set pct = (rec.confidence * 100)|round|int %}
  <div class="card">
    <div class="fix">
      <div class="conf">
        <div class="n">{{ pct }}</div>
        <div class="lbl">confidence</div>
        <div class="track"><div class="fill {{ 'weak' if rec.support != 'Strong' }}" style="width: {{ pct }}%;"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="where">{{ rec.element_label or (rec.element_id|label) }}<span class="tag tag-{{ 'Strong' if rec.support == 'Strong' else 'Weak' }}">{{ "Strong evidence" if rec.support == "Strong" else "Weaker evidence" }}</span></div>
        <div class="fix-text">{{ rec.recommendation|clean }}</div>
        {% if rec.also %}<div class="small">Also consider: {{ rec.also|map("clean")|join(" ") }}</div>{% endif %}
        {% if rec.measurability is defined and rec.measurability < 1 %}
        <div class="small">Confidence lowered from {{ (rec.confidence_raw * 100)|round|int }}: this part of the page is small compared with the tracking error.</div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
<div class="empty">No suggestions passed verification for this session.</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>How we <span class="serif">checked</span></h2>
<p class="lead">Four AI agents worked through this test, each building on the last.</p>
<div class="agents">
  <div class="agent"><b>1 · Behaviour</b>Described what people did on the page.</div>
  <div class="agent"><b>2 · Evaluation</b>Checked it against usability principles: <span class="num">{{ issues|length }}</span> {{ "problem" if issues|length == 1 else "problems" }} kept.</div>
  <div class="agent"><b>3 · Recommendation</b>Drafted <span class="num">{{ recommendations_kept|length + recommendations_rejected|length }}</span> {{ "fix" if (recommendations_kept|length + recommendations_rejected|length) == 1 else "fixes" }}.</div>
  <div class="agent"><b>4 · Critic</b>Kept <span class="num">{{ recommendations_kept|length }}</span>, threw out <span class="num">{{ recommendations_rejected|length }}</span> not backed by the data.</div>
</div>
{% if quality %}
<div class="quality">
  <strong>Tracking quality:</strong>
  {% if quality.gaze_error_px is not none %}
    on average {{ "%.0f"|format(quality.gaze_error_px) }} px ({{ "%.1f"|format(quality.gaze_error_pct_diagonal) }}% of the screen) from the true spot,
    measured by the {{ "accuracy check after calibration" if quality.error_source == "accuracy_check" else "calibration itself" }}.
  {% endif %}
  {% if quality.level == "limited" %}Because accuracy was only fair, no finding is rated above "Worth fixing".{% endif %}
  {% if quality.reasons %}{{ quality.reasons|join("; ") }}.{% endif %}
  {% if quality.low_confidence_elements %}
  <br>Too small to measure reliably at this accuracy: {{ quality.low_confidence_elements|map("label")|list|unique|list|truncate_list(8)|join(", ") }}.
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}
{% if recommendations_rejected %}
<div class="rejected">
  <strong>Thrown out by the critic:</strong>
  {% for rec in recommendations_rejected %}{{ rec.recommendation|clean }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="end">Generated by GazeLens, gaze-driven UX evaluation. Gaze was estimated from an ordinary webcam; treat findings on small elements as indicative.</div>

</body>
</html>
